    "created_at": "2016-10-31T10:18:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-31T10:18:17Z",
    "body": "Why would you want to allow `div` as child element of `dl`?\nXHTML 2 had proposed a `di` element for that purpose: https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml2/mod-list.html#edef_list_di. An earlier draft of HTML5 had included `di` as well. It has been removed later because Hixie had no use for it.\nWhy not introduce `di` now?\nThe problem I see with `div`: for not allowing any content, but just `dt` and `dd` children, another complicated if-then-else rule for its content model is needed. It would be easier with `di`: `dl` may have `di`, `dt` and `dd` children; `di` may have `dt` and `dd` children; `div` can stay as it was.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
