    "body": "I was not aware of use cases that required multiple nested elements (I don't recall it being stated as a requirement in #1937), and so went with the strict and simple approach. Why do you need multiple elements? Can you point to something where you currently use `ul`?\r\n\r\nAllowing arbitrary nested `div`s makes several things more complicated: conformance checkers, learning the language, data mining tools that get the name-value groups (the spec has an algorithm for it), as well as WYSIWYG editors wanting to support this structure.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
